          "unit_id": "the_talk",
          "title": "After the Talk",
          "description": "Deduce lo que es seguro, posible o imposible: must, might, could y can't.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "the_talk_lesson",
              "title": "Modals of deduction: present",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "After the talk",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Ms Martín? Mark Reed, Reed Hotels. That was a terrific talk."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Thank you, Mr Reed. Nice to meet you."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Call me Mark. I'd like Harbour Studio to redesign our websites. All forty-two hotels."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Forty-two? That's… a very big project."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Here's my card. Let's talk next week."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Who was that? He must be important. Did you see his watch?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "He owns a hotel chain. He must have a lot of money."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Reed Hotels? That can't be the company from the TV adverts. They're enormous."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "It might be. He said forty-two hotels."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Then this could be the biggest contract Harbour Studio has ever had."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Helen will be delighted. Or terrified. It could be either."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "She must be waiting for news. Call her now!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "The next morning, Lucía's talk goes well. Afterwards, an American man in an expensive suit is waiting for her near the stage."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"He must be important.\" Daniel is…",
                        "options": [
                          "almost sure it is true",
                          "almost sure it is false",
                          "not sure at all"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"That can't be the company from the TV adverts.\" Daniel thinks it is…",
                        "options": [
                          "impossible",
                          "possible"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"It might be.\" means…",
                        "options": [
                          "quizá",
                          "seguro"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "How many hotels does Mark Reed have?",
                        "options": [
                          "forty-two",
                          "twenty-four",
                          "four"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Modals of deduction: present",
                    "explanation": "Usamos modales para hacer deducciones sobre el presente:\n• must + verbo = estamos casi seguros de que es verdad (= debe de): He must be important.\n• can't + verbo = estamos casi seguros de que no es verdad: That can't be the same company.\n• might / may / could + verbo = es posible: It might be.\n\nOjo: para la deducción negativa se usa can't, no mustn't (que significa prohibición).\n\nCon acciones en curso: must be + -ing: She must be waiting for news.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Modal",
                        "Certeza",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "must",
                          "casi seguro que sí",
                          "He must be important."
                        ],
                        [
                          "might / may / could",
                          "posible",
                          "It might be the same company."
                        ],
                        [
                          "can't",
                          "casi seguro que no",
                          "That can't be the same company."
                        ],
                        [
                          "must be + -ing",
                          "deducción sobre algo en curso",
                          "She must be waiting for news."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "He must be important. Did you see his watch?",
                      "That can't be the company from the TV adverts.",
                      "This could be the biggest contract Harbour Studio has ever had.",
                      "She must be waiting for news."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
